  "title": "Moms Describe Their First Ultrasound in Just 3 Words",
  "h1": "",
  "headings": [],
  "content_body": "Ultrasounds are a regular part of pregnancy, but that first one is particularly special. It's the first time you'll get to see your growing little one (even if they just look like a little tadpole!) and the first time you'll hear their little heartbeat. So we asked moms to describe what they thought when they first saw baby on that screen. Here's what they had to stay:\n\n\"That's a Baby?\"\n\n\"Yay, a Heartbeat\"\n\n\"Tears of Joy!\"\n\n\"That's in There?\"\n\n\"It's a ... Tadpole!\"\n\n\"My Little Blessing\"\n\n\"My Poor Bladder\"\n\n\"Where Is It?\"\n\n\"There are Two?!\"\n\n\"This Feels Real\"\n\n\"Cute Little Alien\"\n\n\"Nervous, Scared, Anxious\"\n\n\"Blew Me Away\"\n\n\"I'm a Mom!\"\n\n\"That's My Baby!\"",
